<title>USA: Repligen identifies growth inhibitor.</title>
<headline>Repligen identifies growth inhibitor.</headline>
<dateline>NEEDHAM, Mass. 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Repligen Corp said Friday that it has identified a novel, small molecule inhibitor of two growth factors: basic fibroblast growth factor (bFGF) and vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF).</p>
<p>These factors are key initiators of angiogenesis, a process of uncontrolled blood vessel proliferation believed to be important in solid tumor growth and certain ocular diseases such as diabetic retinopathy.</p>
<p>According to Repligen, the compound blocks the interaction of the growth factors with heparin-like carbohydrates (&quot;glyceptors&quot;) found on the surface of blood vessel (endothelial) cells.</p>
</text>
